// ============================================
// Detection: Successful Sign-In from New IP Address
// Source: Microsoft Sentinel Analytics Rule
// ============================================
//
// Description:
// This detection identifies successful sign-in activity from an unfamiliar,
// low-frequency, or newly observed IP address.
//
// It is designed to surface potentially suspicious authentication behavior
// where the source IP differs from the user's recent sign-in history.
//
// Trigger Logic:
// - Monitors Entra ID sign-in activity
// - Focuses on successful sign-ins in the recent detection window
// - Compares recent sign-ins against historical sign-in activity
// - Flags activity from an IP address not commonly or previously associated
//   with the user
//
// Why This Matters:
// Suspicious or unfamiliar IP-based sign-ins can indicate:
// - Unauthorized access attempts
// - Use of compromised credentials
// - Login activity from unexpected devices or locations
// - Abnormal authentication patterns requiring investigation
//
// IP-based detections add important context even when the login itself is successful.
//
// Analyst Notes:
// - Review whether the IP address is expected for the user
// - Compare the IP against recent and historical sign-in behavior
// - Check for other suspicious activity tied to the same account
// - Review authentication timing, frequency, and follow-on behavior
// - Escalate if the sign-in appears inconsistent with normal user activity
//
// Expected Outcome:
// This rule generates an alert in Microsoft Sentinel when suspicious
// sign-in activity from a new or unfamiliar IP is identified.
// The alert is grouped into an incident for analyst investigation.
//
// ============================================
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(1h)
| where ResultType == 0
| join kind=leftanti (
    SigninLogs
    | where TimeGenerated between (ago(7d) .. ago(1h))
    | summarize by UserPrincipalName, IPAddress
) on UserPrincipalName, IPAddress
| project TimeGenerated, UserPrincipalName, IPAddress, AppDisplayName
// ============================================
